UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 7, Week 10, Lesson 3: Using evidence and quotes', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Using evidence means weaving short quotations with quotation marks, using ellipsis carefully when shortening and citing chapter or page per class rules. Prefer brief phrases over huge block quotes in paragraphs.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nEmbed and cite: the words Not yet wait for the siren to fade as a short quote.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included.\n\nCHECK\nChanging quote words to fit your claim. Accuracy is non-negotiable.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nProduce five embedded quotations from your novel with citations and one-sentence explanations each.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Using evidence means weaving short quotations with quotation marks, using ellipsis carefully when shortening and citing chapter or page per class rules. Prefer brief phrases over huge block quotes in paragraphs.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Language and vocabulary","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN4-ECB-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Produce five embedded quotations from your novel with citations and one-sentence explanations each. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Strong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included. Reasoning: I used quotation marks by attending to ellipsis rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Changing quote words to fit your claim. Accuracy is non-negotiable. Correction: Strong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included. Why: the correction restores accurate use of quotation marks.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Changing quote words to fit your claim. Accuracy is non-negotiable. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating quotation marks on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with quotation marks, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Strong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included. This matches the lesson skill for quotation marks.","options":["Changing quote words to fit your claim. Accuracy is non-negotiable.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Strong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included."],"question":"Embed and cite: the words Not yet wait for the siren to fade as a short quote. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanati