he siren to fade as a short quote.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: Correct marks, optional ellipsis if shortened fairly, citation included.","explain":"Using evidence means weaving short quotations with quotation marks, using ellipsis carefully when shortening and citing chapter or page per class rules. Prefer brief phrases over huge block quotes in paragraphs.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Changing quote words to fit your claim. Accuracy is non-negotiable. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Using quotations.","caption":"Weave, do not dump.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Short quote</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">phrase</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Cite</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">ch / page</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Weak: pasting five sentences. Strong: Maya whispers, ''Not yet…'' (ch.3), showing delayed action. Ellipsis marks omitted w Then write your own attempt.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Weak: pasting five sentences. Strong: Maya whispers, ''Not yet…'' (ch.3), showing delayed action. Ellipsis marks omitted w Then write your own attempt."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader. A supported explanation follows the actual words and purpose of the task.","options":["A claim unrelated to the text.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no explanation.","Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about quotation marks?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nWeak: pasting five sentences. Strong: Maya whispers, ''Not yet…'' (ch.3), showing delayed action. Ellipsis marks omitted words without twisting meaning. Think about how this word or relationship creates meaning.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUnderline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","explain":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on